cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the paper and the software as below."
title: "Imputation of missing locations in time-use surveys: code and aggregate results"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Code and aggregate results of the paper "Imputation of missing locations in time-use surveys".
  The pipeline imputes the places of activities missing from the German diaries of the 2010 round
  of the Harmonised European Time Use Surveys (HETUS) from the 13 countries that record them, with
  a Markov chain over activity episodes; tests the imputation by imputing each of these countries
  from the others; and runs a global sensitivity analysis over the full factorial of modelling
  choices, coding assumptions, random draws and transfer errors between countries, with exact
  Sobol' and optimal-transport indices. The repository holds the code, the settings and the
  aggregate results of the run behind the paper, the script that builds its figures and tables
  and an end-to-end test on synthetic data. The HETUS scientific use files,
  which Eurostat provides to approved research projects, are not included.
